 "report_kind": "aggregation-score-report",
 "output_schema": "command-center/schema/receipt.schema.json",
 "claim": "On N=200 held-out resolved cases of the TST-0288 deterministic gold set (production council corpus ABSENT; live B07 paths absent: ['tools/council/simulate.py', 'tools/council/vote/bayes.py', 'tools/council/vote/weights.py', 'tools/council/vote/tally.py', 'command-center/receipts/TST-0287.json', 'command-center/receipts/TST-0280.json']), weighted and Bayesian aggregation do not outperform unweighted majority (calibration-weighted and log-pool Brier are higher, not lower); the extra machinery is unjustified complexity on this gold set and the default must be unweighted majority, not weighted or Bayesian pooling. Best-by-Brier is abstention at 0.045960 (95% bootstrap CI 0.038172–0.053968) versus majority 0.053980 (CI 0.045816–0.062551); mean paired Brier difference (method−majority)=-0.008019, two-sided permutation p=0.0027, majority−best=0.008019. Weight-source ablation: calibration-weighted Brier=0.102562, role-weighted Brier=0.104678.",
 "verdict": "WEIGHTED-AND-BAYESIAN-DO-NOT-BEAT-MAJORITY",
